1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:07,950
So first I made a quick stop at Portobello Market, which is a little outdoor market full of food and clothes and plants that I had to exercise all my willpower not to buy.
先去了波托贝洛市集，一个有食物、衣服和植物的小小露天市场。我得用尽意志力，才忍住没买那些植物。

2
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:14,280
Unfortunately since I filmed this on a Monday, only a couple clothing stalls were out, but I've heard that there are a lot more on the weekends.
可惜拍摄这天是周一，出来摆摊卖衣服的只有几家，不过听说周末会多得多。

3
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:20,760
I did think the corduroy collar on this jacket was super cute, mainly just because I have an unhealthy obsession with corduroy.
我倒是觉得这件外套的灯芯绒领子特别可爱，主要是因为我实在太迷灯芯绒了。

4
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:23,470
But ultimately I didn't find anything here to take home.
但最后还是没有在这里找到想带回家的东西。

5
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:27,240
So next I arrived at the vintage motherland, Goldsmith Vintage.
接着，我到了复古衣服的天堂，Goldsmith Vintage。

6
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:34,120
Now this store's reputation precedes it. Everyone from my Airbnb host to you guys on Instagram had recommended checking this place out.
这家店早就名声在外了，从民宿房东到 Instagram 上的你们，都推荐我来逛逛。

7
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:38,479
The curation was … out of this world, but so were the prices, unfortunately.
选品真是绝了，可惜价格也同样高得惊人。

8
00:00:39,159 --> 00:00:42,760
Now one thing that really caught my eye was their selection of vintage denim.
特别吸引我的，是这里的复古牛仔服饰。

9
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:49,159
I swear finding a good pair of vintage jeans is harder than finding a good boy on Tinder, but that sure as hell does not stop me from trying.
说真的，找一条好看的复古牛仔裤，简直比在 Tinder 上找个好男孩还难，但这可挡不住我继续试。

10
00:00:49,159 --> 00:00:52,920
I tried on a few pairs here, but alas neither of them are getting a second date.
我在这里试了几条，可惜，都没有下一次约会的机会。

11
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:54,920
Um, they were just not the perfect fit.
嗯，就是没有那么合身。

12
00:00:54,920 --> 00:01:03,720
I found a couple Disney tops that I thought were really cute, but I felt like they wouldn't really integrate with my current wardrobe very well since they were a little bit in your face 90s.
我还看到几件挺可爱的迪士尼上衣，但感觉很难融入现在的衣橱，因为它们的九十年代风格太鲜明了。

13
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:12,750
And I found a denim jacket that I really liked that I may or may not have decided to purchase. You'll find out at the end.
还看到一件我很喜欢的牛仔外套。至于到底买没买，留到最后揭晓。

14
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:15,400
Next I made a quick round of some charity shops.
接着，又快速逛了几家慈善旧衣店。

15
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:19,160
Charity shops are England's closest equivalent to American thrift stores.
慈善商店大概是英国最接近美国二手旧货店的地方。

16
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:26,680
Prices are really affordable, around 3 to 10 pounds, and the proceeds go to a charitable cause such as cancer research or children's hospitals.
价格挺亲民，大约三到十英镑，所得会用于慈善用途，比如癌症研究或儿童医院。

17
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:31,639
I found them really well organized, but as many of you warned me, the pickings are a bit slim.
我觉得这些店整理得很有条理，不过正如很多人提醒的，可挑的东西确实不算多。

18
00:01:31,639 --> 00:01:38,680
I saw a lot of great basics like sweaters and cardigans and jeans, but was out of luck finding anything with that special vintage pizzazz.
基本款倒是很多，比如毛衣、开衫和牛仔裤，但没找到那种特别有复古味道的东西。

19
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:42,840
I don't know if anybody says pizzazz anymore. Just me, apparently.
也不知道现在还有没有人用 pizzazz 这个词，看来就我还在用了。

20
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:45,240
I did find one charity shop that I loved.
不过，我确实找到了一家特别喜欢的慈善商店。

21
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:57,480
The Royal Trinity Hospice on Portobello Road was super well organized and had a surprising number of designer items, like these insane 70s Dolce Gama heels that have a freaking corduroy butterfly on them.
波托贝洛路上的 Royal Trinity Hospice 店铺整理得特别好，设计师款也多得让人意外，比如这双七十年代风格的高跟鞋，上面还有灯芯绒蝴蝶。

22
00:01:57,480 --> 00:02:00,269
I, that isn't the perfect shoe, I don't know what is.
要是这都不算完美的鞋，那我真不知道什么才算了。

23
00:02:00,279 --> 00:02:03,880
Unfortunately they were too small for me, but I had a look around at everything else.
可惜它们对我来说太小了，所以我又看了看其他东西。

24
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:08,520
The manager of this store, turns out, was actually a subscriber as well, and she was absolutely lovely.
没想到，这家店的经理也是我的订阅观众，而且人特别好。

25
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:14,440
She's clearly very good at her job because the store was amazing, and she gave me a bunch of other recommendations for where to shop next.
她显然很擅长这份工作，店铺很棒，还给我推荐了好多接下来可以逛的地方。

26
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:17,559
Anyways, here is me making a fool out of myself in the fitting room.
总之，接下来就是我在试衣间里瞎折腾的画面。

27
00:02:17,559 --> 00:02:20,680
First I decided to try on this pastel pink blazer.
先试试这件浅粉色西装外套。

28
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:28,600
Now I feel like if Lady Gaga wore this on the red carpet with her Joanne hat and like a little bit of cleavage, she would look … amazing.
我觉得，要是 Lady Gaga 穿着它走红毯，再配上 Joanne 那顶帽子，稍微露一点领口，一定会很惊艳。

29
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:32,040
But at last I am not Lady Gaga, and it was just a little bit baggy on me.
但可惜我不是 Lady Gaga，这件穿在我身上还是有点松垮。

30
00:02:32,040 --> 00:02:38,430
I also tried on a couple Mean Girls worthy pink cardigans and decided that this pastel one was indeed so fetch.
我还试了几件很有《贱女孩》风格的粉色开衫，觉得这件浅色的确实很有范儿。

31
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:45,480
I picked up this dress from the designer section. I was … crazy about the corset detail, but I wasn't crazy about the fit.
我从设计师款区域拿了这条裙子，特别喜欢它的束身细节，但对版型没那么满意。

32
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:48,600
So I was trying to figure out if it was something I could alter.
所以我在想，能不能自己把它改一改。

33
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:52,840
And for some goddamn reason I decided to try on these heart shaped pajama pants.
然后，不知道怎么想的，我又去试了这条爱心图案的睡裤。

34
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:58,590
I think they were actually by a designer brand like Chloe or something, so I was like, they've gotta look good on me.
我觉得这好像还是 Chloé 之类的设计师品牌，所以当时就想：穿在身上肯定得好看吧。

35
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:01,639
They don't look good on me. Anyways, moving on.
结果并不好看。好啦，继续下一家。

36
00:03:01,639 --> 00:03:05,400
Lastly I hopped on a bus to a charity shop called Trade in Shepherd's Bush.
最后，我坐公交去了 Shepherd’s Bush 一家叫 Trade 的慈善商店。

37
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:11,880
Now I guess I unintentionally saved the best for last because this turned out to be by far my favorite thrift store that I went to that day.
看来我无意中把最好的留到了最后，因为这家成了我那天最喜欢的旧衣店。

38
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:20,759
The prices were all under 20 pounds. There was a huge selection, and I found some really unique and funky vintage pieces that I will show you in my haul here.
价格都在二十英镑以下，选择也很多。我淘到了几件特别、有趣的复古衣服，接下来的购物分享里给你们看。
